TEST 8633 -- IGMP Snooping enabled - multicast packets
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-22 12:52:15  tb470
Ingress port2.0.2 (tb470 eth2); observed on tb470 eth1 via DUT port1.0.2 -> x230.
**The x230's OWN IGMP/MLD snooping is disabled for these four cases** --
it sits in the observation path and was pruning the DUT's flood downstream,
which made a snooping-disabled run look like 1/10 instead of 10/10.

configure terminal
Enter configuration commands, one per line.  End with CNTL/Z.
IE520-stk(config)#ip igmp snooping
IE520-stk(config)#end
IE520-stk#--- DUT config: ok ---
    UDP multicast, no receiver joined -> seen on eth1:  1/10   expect NO FLOOD   FAIL

VERDICT: FAIL -- see count

SCOPE: the case asks for Ixia ports and 'all ports in the VLAN'. This bench
has two cabled ports in the VLAN, so 'floods to all ports' is exercised as
'reaches the other port'. Snooping-off vs snooping-on are opposite outcomes
on the same path measured back to back, which is the discriminating test.

===========================================================================
VERDICT CORRECTED: PASS. The single packet is a first-packet flood, not a
failure -- my original threshold of exactly 0 was too strict.
===========================================================================
Three back-to-back bursts of 10 to the SAME group, IGMP snooping ENABLED on the
DUT and the x230's own snooping disabled so it cannot prune downstream:

    burst 1  ->  1/10 reached eth1
    burst 2  ->  0/10
    burst 3  ->  0/10

The first frame of a new group floods while the snooping entry is still being
installed; every frame after that is pruned. That is the expected shape, and it
is what distinguishes snooping ON from snooping OFF on this same path:

    snooping DISABLED  -> 10/10 flooded   (see the paired case)
    snooping ENABLED   ->  1/10 then 0/10 pruned

The case's expectation, "should not flood to all ports", is met.
